/**
@page licensing_and_provenance Licensing and provenance

@tableofcontents

@section license_matrix Licence matrix

| Part | Licence | Text |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Library code (`include/`, `lib/`, `ld/`, `mk/`) | LGPL-3.0-or-later | `LICENSE`, `COPYING.LGPL3` |
| `scripts/checkpatch.pl` | GPL-2.0-only | `COPYING.GPL2` |
| `lib/ble/wch/` and `include/libopenwch/ble/wch/` | Apache-2.0 | `lib/ble/wch/LICENSE` |
| Project documentation and governance files | CC0-1.0 / public domain | `README.md`, `NOTICE`, `HACKING` |
| Doxygen Awesome theme under `doc/awesome/` | MIT | `doc/awesome/LICENSE` |

Applications that merely link against libopenwch are unaffected by the LGPL,
as with libopencm3.  The vendored WCH BLE stack is a separate work and keeps
its own Apache-2.0 terms.

@section license_ble WCH BLE binary

`lib/ble/wch/LIBCH58xBLE.a` and the matching vendor header are redistributed
verbatim from WCH's CH583 SDK under Apache-2.0.  They are not LGPL.  The
wrapper in `lib/ble/*.c` and `include/libopenwch/ble/*.h` is original to
libopenwch and stays LGPL-3.0-or-later.

@section license_upstream Derived from libopencm3

The build system, directory conventions, linker-script skeleton, several
scripts, and the Doxygen/header conventions are derived from libopencm3 and
remain under the LGPL.  Individual copyright notices are retained.

@section license_consulted Consulted as documentation only

WCH's official EVT packages for the CH32V003 and CH583 were read to establish
register addresses, bit positions, field layouts, and clock/flash ordering.
No EVT source code was copied.  ch32fun influenced the toolchain strategy and
supplied protocol facts; no ch32fun source was copied.

@section license_details Full notice

The repository root `NOTICE` contains the complete provenance record.  The
family sites also include this licence page through
<a href="../ch32v0/html/lgpl_license.html">CH32V00x</a> and
<a href="../ch5xx58x/html/lgpl_license.html">CH58x</a>.
*/
